1
00:00:03,249 --> 00:00:05,237
Open Tools, Time Zones.

2
00:00:05,237 --> 00:00:07,019
Each row is one map:

3
00:00:07,019 --> 00:00:11,818
its name, the time zone it stands for, who created it, and when.

4
00:00:11,818 --> 00:00:14,629
The Search box finds a map by name.

5
00:00:21,475 --> 00:00:23,396
Click Add Time Zone Map.

6
00:00:23,396 --> 00:00:27,815
The Name is what people will see, for example Mexico City Time.

7
00:00:28,313 --> 00:00:34,818
Choose the Time zone the name stands for, here America slash Mexico City, and click Save.

8
00:00:34,818 --> 00:00:39,953
Each name can be used once, and each time zone can have only one map.

9
00:00:40,404 --> 00:00:42,447
The new map is on the list.

10
00:00:42,447 --> 00:00:45,480
Edit points a map at a different time zone.

11
00:00:45,480 --> 00:00:49,319
The name is fixed after you save it, so to rename a map,

12
00:00:49,319 --> 00:00:51,424
delete it and add a new one.

